  "instructions": [
    "Step 0 (idle): Start begins a batch only while StopPB is TRUE, HoldPB is FALSE, LevelHigh is FALSE and InletOpen is FALSE.",
    "Step 1 (open inlet): InletValve on until InletOpen reports the open position.",
    "Step 2 (fill): keep InletValve on until LevelHigh.",
    "Step 3 (close inlet): InletValve off; continue when InletOpen is FALSE and LevelLow is FALSE.",
    "Step 4 (drain): DrainPump on until LevelLow.",
    "Step 5 (complete): outputs off; StartPB returns to step 0 for the next batch.",
    "In steps 1 to 4, HoldPB sets Held: both outputs off and the step stays. StartPB clears Held and the same step continues.",
    "StopPB FALSE (Stop pressed) returns to step 0 from every step and clears Held.",
    "Open the Sequence tab: it shows the active step, what it waits for, permissives, interlocks, step timers and the history."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Handle Stop first, then HOLD, then the CASE: skip the CASE while Held is TRUE.",
    "Write the outputs after the CASE from Step and Held: InletValve := (Step = 1 OR Step = 2) AND NOT Held;",
    "If Start does nothing, the Sequence tab lists the permissive or interlock that refuses it."
  ],
  "knowledgeRefs": [
    "fundamentals.sequences",
    "fundamentals.interlocks"
  ],
